            "review_text": "Handi Suyadi\nBandung, Indonesia911 contributions\n0\nAt Least Try to be Authentic\nJun 2019 • Family\nAt the first night in Ho Chi Minh City, I had dinner at Saigon3. Looking the menu was Chinese Food (certain menu was fusion with Vietnamese food, but most of them also seem authentic to cater actual Chinese people), everyone though would have taste like most Chinese Food.\n\nMost of them yes although have soft taste, with sole exception stir fried bean sprout which have bland flavor. The menu wasn't even seem added any spice. Regardless of bland stir fried bean sprout, the rest of them actually taste good.\n\nFor those miss Chinese Food during holiday or life at Ho Chi Minh City, Saigon3 could be one of the alternative.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten June 13, 2019",
