            "review_text": "sunraygrill\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam340 contributions\n0\nHighs and Lows\nFeb 2018 • Family\nThe place offers Cantonese standards at prices that don't break the bank. Nothing fancy here it's a plain and basic dining area, hanging meats, tanks of fish (mostly low end varieties) and standard Vietnamese service. \n\nThe roast meats and vegetables were best bests. We had the roast pork. Dumplings were not so refined and less stellar. Many stuffed with bits of hard and gristly meat parts. Flavors and textures lacking compared to my expectations on dim sum.\n\nOverall not a bad stop if you cherry pick the menu. But that would take a few more tries to get a deeper look and I'm not sure if I'll do that. Many better yet more expensive options but worth it for me.\nRead more\nWritten February 11, 2018",
